{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of design and siting, would appear at odds with the prevailing character of the immediate area and planned form of the original estate. The proposal would result in a detrimental loss of symmetry to the block of flats. It would cause undue harm to the character and appearance of the area and present poor design, contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character and are high-quality:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policies D4 of the London Plan (March 2021) Policies SP2 and DMD1 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)",
    "The proposed development, by reason of siting and scale,&nbsp;would result a loss of outlook and privacy to neighbouring occupiers.&nbsp;The proposal would unacceptably harm residential amenity, thereby constituting&nbsp;unneighbourly&nbsp;development contrary to:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2024)Policy&nbsp;D6 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMD1 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)",
    "In the absence of further information&nbsp;on the proposed parking and access arrangements, the proposal&nbsp;fails to demonstrate whether sufficient car parking provision would be made or whether this could be&nbsp;adequately accommodated in the surrounding area. In the absence of such, the proposal is found to result in unacceptable parking stress and congestion in the vicinity of the application site.&nbsp; As such, it fails to comply with the following policies:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2024)Policies T1 and T6.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMT2 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)"
  ],
